  "title": "tap-oran: address memory management issues",
  "description": "Add a finish function to the call of `register_tap_listener()` which\nfrees the memory allocated by the tap. This includes the tap data\nallocated upon registration, as well as the list of flows.\n\nAdd code to the reset function which frees the memory allocated for\nflows, instead of simply leaking them by resetting the list pointer to\n`NULL`.\n\nIn `oran_stat_packet()`, sort and iterate over `hs->flow_list` directly,\nbypassing the temporary variable `list`. All operations on `GList`s,\nincluding `g_list_sort()`, return a pointer to the new start of the\nlist; thus, without this change, only `list` is valid and\n`hs->flow_list` becomes a stale pointer after the sort.\n\nPing #20432",
